      "text": "4 Stoic Lessons for a Dark World You've been lied to about how influence really works. Most people miss it because it looks completely normal. That's the point. The most effective tactics hide in plain sight. Cognitive research shows your brain prefers the easy answer — and that preference is exactly what gets used against you. The scariest part? It works silently. No raised voice, no threats — just a pattern repeated until it feels normal. That's the real danger. Follow Cognitive Dark — the dark side of the human mind, decoded daily.",
